#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# riemann_siegel_theta

#% text
# `riemann_siegel_theta(t)` gives the Riemann-Siegel theta function, the phase `im_part(log_gamma(1/4 + im*t/2)) - t*log(pi)/2`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is defined so that `exp(im*theta(t))*zeta(1/2 + im*t)` is real for real `t` (DLMF 25.10.3); it is odd and grows like `t/2*log(t/(2*pi*e))`.

#% item
# Machine numbers and balls give numerical values; `riemann_siegel_theta(0)` is 0.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
riemann_siegel_theta(0)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
riemann_siegel_theta(1.0)
#% output
#= -1.76754795281229

#% cell
riemann_siegel_theta(20.0)
#% output
#= 1.18689480844448

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The definition:

#% cell
riemann_siegel_theta(5.0) - (im_part(log_gamma(0.25 + 2.5*im)) - 5.0*log(pi)/2)
#% output
#= 0.0

